---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Nested Chronometric Architecture" description="The A-B-C-D timeline layers and where dark matter resides.">
  <article class="container" style="padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 4rem; max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>Nested Chronometric Architecture</h1>
    <p class="lead">The universe is not governed by a single, universal clock. Instead, time is structured in overlapping, nested layers that emerged from the initial puncture of the Timeless Sea (TSC). These layers did not end—they continue to exist right now.</p>

    <figure style="margin: 2rem 0; text-align: center; background: #f8fafc; padding: 2rem; border-radius: 12px; border: 1px dashed #cbd5e1;">
      <div style="font-size: 1.2rem; color: #64748b; font-style: italic;">
      <img
        src="/images/Nested_Chronometric_Architecture_Diagram.png"
        alt="Hydrodynamic Particle Map: Dual-dial topology showing intersection depth (mass) and tilt (charge)" 
        style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);" 
        loading="lazy"
       />
      </div>
      <figcaption style="margin-top: 0.5rem; font-size: 0.9rem; color: #475569;">Fig 1. The Void (Phase B) encapsulates Threshold Time (Phase C), which encapsulates Local Time (Phase D). Dark matter resides in the uncoupled Threshold layer.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <h2>The Four Chronometric Layers</h2>
    <ul style="line-height: 1.8; color: #334155;">
      <li><strong>Phase A (The Spark):</strong> The initial event where the timeline hypersurface (Σ) first punctures the static TSC. This topological instability nucleates the sweep we perceive as the Big Bang.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase B (The Void):</strong> The initial shockwave creates pure Expansion Time. Crucially, the Void is not just a past phase; it is the enclosing spatial environment for all subsequent evolution.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase C (The Fringe):</strong> A slow frame-rate layer forms inside the Void. Particles here experience shallow coupling to the timeline sweep.</li>
      <li><strong>Phase D (The Ignition):</strong> Where matter density crosses a critical threshold inside Phase C, Local Time ignites (the CMB epoch). This is the fast frame-rate layer where we currently exist.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Overlap: Where Dark Matter Lives</h2>
    <p>Threshold Time (Phase C) does not end when Local Time (Phase D) begins. When Local Time ignited in dense pockets, not all particles crossed the threshold. Particles in the sparse outskirts remained locked in the shallow-coupled state of the Threshold Time layer.</p>
    <p>This overlapping, uncoupled population is <strong>Dark Matter</strong>. It possesses mass (hydrodynamic resistance) but exhibits zero electric charge because it remains geometrically locked in a state that prevents interaction with our local electromagnetic baseline.</p>
    
    <div style="margin-top: 2rem; padding: 1.5rem; background: #eff6ff; border-left: 4px solid #3b82f6; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;">
      <h3 style="margin-top: 0; color: #1e40af;">Visual Summary</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0; color: #1e3a8a;">Reality is a nested structure: a layer of Local Time, wrapped inside a layer of Threshold Time, wrapped inside the expansive Void. The mechanical friction between these layers produces the phenomena we measure as gravity and expansion.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>